The CG-mounted baseline has pooled 3-D displacement RMS of
\SI{0.494}{m} and maximum pooled
roll/pitch RMS of \SI{0.228}{\degree}.
Table~\ref{tab:imu-lever-arm} reports the worst canonical direction at each
installation distance.  At \SI{30}{cm} the rotational term
reaches \SI{0.054}{\meter\per\second\squared} RMS in the worst
direction. The largest unmodeled 3-D displacement ratio is
\num{1.001} times the CG
baseline in the port direction, and the largest tilt
ratio is \num{1.025} in the
vertical direction.  Modelling the same lever arm inside
the filter subtracts its rotational force: with exact angular kinematics the largest 3-D ratio over
the three directions is \num{1.000}, and with the deployable
model driven by the measured rate it is
\num{1.000}, leaving only
\SI{0.022}{\meter\per\second\squared} of the injected term
behind. The attitude channel is reported separately:
the worst tilt ratio is \num{0.999} under the exact model
and \num{1.007} under the deployable one.  The installation penalty
depends on the interaction with existing residuals; force subtraction need not improve every error metric.

